From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:14:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] games/acnh: an adaptive-view adapter on the frame step state
 page

On a picture taller than 16:9 the game reuses projections and screen rectangles
it cached before the shape changed, so scissors, captures, field ranges and the
inline keyboard keep their 16:9 positions. The screen-shape stubs change the
output size and camera angle but cannot invalidate those cached objects.

Register an owned ARM64 adapter (view.s, assembled by gen_view_stubs.py,
MIT-0) from the profile's FRAME_STEP callback, for the 3.0.3 main build only:
21 hooks and 29 cache checks refresh cached projections, follow the current
perspective in scissors and captures, widen field ranges and near-plane
unprojection, and dock the inline keyboard and footer. It shares dm_fps_state
with screen_shape (+0x58 target aspect, +0xa0..+0xb8 frame stamps), so no VIEW
table, VIEW_STATE_OFF, host file or general-code change is needed.

main+0x265140 is the one shared site: a single chained stub runs the upstream
y-row division first (its 16:9 test reads m0/m5, which the adapter's
Lscreen_projection rewrites) then calls the adapter's keyboard dock. The stub
saves x30 with x0: the bl overwrites x30 with its own return address, and a
stub that saved only x0 returned to the instruction after that bl and walked
the stack up a page per pass. main+0x27d4c0 and main+0x27d570 were
disassembled and coexist.

The frame stamps are values in the free part of the state page, with no host
pointer: +0xa8 is the host's present counter, +0xb0 the keyboard frame's stamp
and +0xb8 a touch panel's. dm_guest_frame_tick advances +0xa8 each present.
Lrecent_keyboard reads +0xb0, so the dock never ran while the stamps went to
+0x28 / +0x38, and _dm_view_keyboard_window dereferenced the counter as a
pointer.

The stubs' branches name a label and are encoded from the stub's own layout
(nso_asm CBZ / TBZ / BCOND) instead of a hand-counted word offset: the 0x265140
stub grew by three instructions, and a stale +41 would have branched into the
ldp before the ret, popping 16 bytes the stub never pushed. test_view_stubs
checks that every conditional branch of every stub the profile emits lands
inside that stub, and that duo_anchor.c's __text is still the words pasted
into patches.py.

Checked: the rewritten 3.0.3 main from its original NSO is byte-identical to
the image validated on the device, as are fixups.tsv, sites.tsv and cuts.tsv;
test_patches, test_view_stubs and test_docs pass (38); both new tests fail when
their defect is reintroduced. Not checked: a device run of the dock offset's
stretch division (option B) and of the pointer-free keyboard frame stamps.

(cherry picked from commit 5c91e2a2e608a4ceb3d3aa512e75511391161e25)

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2609
Reason: A wider-than-16:9 iPhone picture keeps its own shape, its touches land on the control they touch, and Animal Crossing: New Horizons refreshes the projections it cached at 16:9
Issue: none

